"P1603670270" "Talk to Ruth Chandler."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4221119744" "Ruth Chandler can give you some more information about the invention system."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2083767390" "Dr. Taylor showed you the invention tables?   Oh great!  Here are some facts that you may want to keep in mind while you are inventing enhancements.<br><br>The strength of the invented enhancement won't change. Don't worry about out-leveling your slotted enhancement, because it will <b>always</b> give you the bonus it was created at. You can always slot your enhancement up to three levels higher than your current level, but it give you any more of a bonus than it normally would.<br><br>Not only are recipes available to you at the universities and crafting tables, enemies can drop them along with invention salvage. These recipes can be used with all your salvage for better inventions and costume pieces. Keep an eye out for them because, like Inspirations, they can only be used once and then will disappear. Go chat with Dr. Topffer.  He'll tell you about some special enhancement sets and what they can do for you.<br><br>The invented enhancements are level based so you'll never outgrow your created enhancement. You can create invented enhancements up to a maximum of three levels higher than your current level. Also, your Origin is completely irrelevant.<br><br>The Uncommon and Rare enhancements can also use recipes that are dropped by enemies that you defeat along the way. These recipes will help you invent better enhancements than the invention tables can offer. You can view your different recipes in the recipe tab located in the salvage window.<br><img src=COH_Inv_Inventory.tga><br><br><color deepskyblue>The invented enhancements are not level-based so you'll never outgrow your created enhancement. You can invent enhancements up to a maximum of three levels higher than your current level. Also, your Origin is completely irrelevant. The Uncommon and Rare enhancements can also use recipes that are dropped by enemies that you defeat along the way. These recipes will help you invent better enhancements than the invention tables can offer. </color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2.5_Inv_Tutorial_Compound1_Part7 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2915025384" "Talk to Dr. Rudolph Topffer"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2783656234" "Dr. Rudolph Topffer will help you complete your training in invention crafting."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3028502561" "Ruth explained to you the special enhancement sets that can be created.  Now let me tell you a little more about these very useful sets, called Powersets. There are some enhancements that work together within a power to give you special bonuses; the more you have the better the bonus.  A nice thing about Uncommon and Rare crafted enhancements is that even though the effect is lower than a Common crafted enhancement, they have multiple results.  Let's take the Bonesnap set for example<br><img src=COH_Inv_Bonesnap.tga><br><br>Uncommon and Rare enhancements are used in these special powersets. When slotting these special crafted enhancements you will gain multiple permanent benefits. A powerset can use as little as three enhancements up to all six, but can only be slotted with other enhancements of the same set.  Keep in mind that these specific sets do have level and power limitations.<br><br>The set bonuses will give you a powerful advantage when used correctly. When these enhancement sets are slotted in the same power, they create a bonus that will always be active. You can have as many enhancement sets as you have available powers. Another nice thing about these particular sets is that as soon as you slot these enhancements the advantage is overall, not just for the power that the crafted enhancement is located in.<br><img src=COH_Inv_Bone_Slot.tga><br><br><color deepskyblue>The Uncommon and Rare crafted enhancements slot into Powersets, which give you multiple permanent benefits.  When these enhancement sets are slotted in the same power, they create a bonus that affects your overall character, not just that specific power. You can have as many enhancement sets as you have available powers. Keep in mind that you don't need to have the power activated to receive the bonus.</color>"

